    "plain": "Expanding the British Business Bank aims to close funding gaps for SMEs and crowd in private investment, with a track record suggesting real economic gains \u2014 but most benefits take years to materialise and projections come largely from the BBB itself.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the BBB can genuinely crowd in private capital at scale or whether institutional and regional barriers (pension fund reluctance, regional risk premia) prevent projected GVA and job gains from materialising.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "tier": "measurable",
        "claim": "The BBB has historically supported over 200,000 businesses, contributing an estimated 250,000 jobs and \u00a343 billion of GVA.",
        "evidence_id": "E9",
